# REQUIRES: python-api, torch
# The frame evaluator as an operation of PyTorch, mdir.torch.evaluate
# (D240, docs/python-frames.md), on the CPU,
# Inputs/python_frames.py: the gradient of a reweighted average of a
# Lennard-Jones mixture from autograd against the covariance formed from
# the evaluator's arrays; the backward by a second pass; gradcheck; a fit
# of one parameter to a synthetic target; the refusals of the adapter; and
# torch.compile. The feature `torch` is set when the interpreter of the
# tests imports torch, or when lit is given -Dtorch_python=<an interpreter
# with torch>.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/pair_tail_system.py %t 60 60 32 3.7 0.5
# RUN: %torch_python %S/Inputs/python_frames.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide torch CPU Double %t | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=CHECK,DOUBLE -DMODE="CPU Double"
# RUN: %torch_python %S/Inputs/python_frames.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide torch CPU Mixed %t | FileCheck %s -DMODE="CPU Mixed"
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the gradient of the reweighted average from autograd against the covariance of the arrays
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: with the Jacobian not kept, the backward by a second pass
# DOUBLE: [[MODE]]: torch.autograd.gradcheck of the reweighted average: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: a fit to the average at sigma* = 0.3705 nm from 0.3700: sigma' = 0.370{{[45]}}
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: refused: a backward through the virial and through a column that the tunable enters, a second backward, positions that require a gradient
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: with the dependent terms alone, the gradient of the reweighted average against that of the whole potential
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: under torch.compile (aot_eager), the same average and gradient: True
# CHECK: torch passed
